// A type declared OUTSIDE the cycle and mirrored by TWO co-tenants of the
// merged package. Nothing here is an existential; this file exists for the
// alias-collision arm alone.
//
// A mirror is named by an alias (foreign.go's aliasOwner), and that alias must
// be declared once per merged package, not once per file. A merged package is
// one strongly-connected component, so two co-tenants mirroring this one type
// would otherwise declare the alias twice in one namespace.
//
// `tests/15-app-and-defer/effects/` has this shape: its `dev`/`prod`/`test`
// co-tenants each mirror `log.ProdLogger`, `console.StdConsole` and
// `clocks.FakeClock` from outside their component. It has nothing to do with
// interfaces, which is why it needs its own arm here rather than riding on
// `App`.
//
// This file must NOT import a cycle member, or it joins the component and there
// is no cross-package alias left to collide.
pub struct Stamp {
    s: String
}

pub fn stamp(s: String): Stamp {
    Stamp{s}
}
